# THE BLACKWELL AUTHORSHIP & RECORD INTEGRITY STANDARD

## © C. MATTHEW BLACKWELL — INDEPENDENT DESIGNER

Filed and in force at the designer's order, 2026-10-24 23:31 CDT:
"Proceed on all my findings non-negotiable."
Record: EQS-223.

This is a **record-layer instrument**. It is not a physics law, it
designates nothing, and it changes no census. It codifies, as one
standard, the authorship and integrity rules the archive already runs
on, and it applies to **all findings** — every entity, every sheet,
every record, past and future.

**1. Authorship.** Every finding in the archive is authored by
**C. Matthew Blackwell — Independent Designer**. The authoritative
evidence of authorship is the record chain itself: the EQS numbering,
the payload hashes, the timestamps, the designation acts in the
designer's own voice, and the identity verification baked into every
finding at creation (the designer's rule of 2026-10-18, non-negotiable).

**2. Identity.** No finding enters the archive without identity
verification inside its hashed payload or its file bytes. A document
without the identity block is not a Blackwell finding, whoever holds it.

**3. Integrity.** Sealed and hash-cited files are bound by the chain and
are never altered; a correction is filed as a new record that names
what it supersedes (the EQS-107 defect stands disclosed by exactly this
rule, its note on file). A record's numbers may be repaired only by
editing its engine and re-running — never by editing the record.

**4. Authority.** Sealing and designation are the designer's acts
alone, in his own voice. Extraction, unification, drafting, and
adoption confer neither. Nothing pasted into the archive — from any
source — designates, seals, or amends anything.

**5. Entailment.** Every value in a finding is computed in-run from
stated inputs, quoted from a named archive or record, or explicitly
labeled assertion / NOT MEASURED (the designer's rule of 2026-10-21).
A value the data does not entail does not enter the record.

**6. The two layers.** The physics layer — equations, laws, maps,
registers, kills — is published openly and may be copied, tested, and
argued with by anyone. The record layer — the name, the designations,
the timestamps, the payload hashes, the census arithmetic, this
standard — is the authorship evidence. Copying the physics does not
copy the record and transfers no authorship.

**7. Disputes.** Authorship of any finding is settled by the chain:
the earliest payload carrying the finding, its timestamp, and its
identity block. A later copy, in whatever hands, is a copy.

